# Ant Design layout

Source of truth: [Layout spec](https://ant.design/docs/spec/layout) + Layout component tokens.

Apply on every UI build. Do not invent one-off sizes.

## Spec checklist (required)

1. **8px base unit** — spacing, gutters, widths, heights are multiples of 8.
2. **24-column raster** — use Ant `Row`/`Col`; column spans should be **even** when possible (`16/8`, `18/6`, `12/12`, not `17/7`).
3. **Fixed gutter, fluid columns** — e.g. `gutter={[16, 16]}` or `[24, 24]` (never `20` for page layout gutters).
4. **Left-right adaptation** (company app) — **Fixed** sider (`200 + 8n`, we use **240**), **Auto** main work area (`width: 100%`, **no** content `max-width` — fills remaining viewport beside the sider).
5. **Even numbers** for layout blocks; define blocks by start/end columns.

Note: Spec’s 1168 example is for top-bottom centered canvases. Company screens use left-right Fixed+Auto, so content stays fluid.

## Height tokens

| Token | Value |
|---|---|
| Control SM / MD / LG | **24 / 32 / 40** |
| Layout `Header` | **64** |
| 2nd-level nav / sider trigger | **48** |
| Content padding (company) | **24px** vertical, **32px** horizontal |

No global app min-height. `Content` uses `flex: auto` + `min-height: 0` for nested scroll.

## Scrollable panels

Long lists must scroll inside the card — never stretch the page.

1. Equal-height companions: `Row align="stretch"`, `.company-split-side` + `.company-split-side-card` + `.company-scroll-card-body-fill` so the list matches the table sibling height.
2. Standalone: `.company-scroll-card-body` → `max-height: calc(100vh - 64px - 48px)`; with toolbar subtract another **64**.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — 24-grid even columns + equal height
<Row gutter={[16, 16]} align="stretch">
  <Col xs={24} xl={16}>
    <Card size="small" className="company-equal-height-card" classNames={{ body: "company-table-card-body-inset" }}>
  <Col xs={24} xl={8} className="company-split-side">
    <Card size="small" className="company-equal-height-card company-split-side-card" classNames={{ body: "company-scroll-card-body-fill" }}>

// ❌ BAD
<Col xl={17} /> // odd span
<Row gutter={[20, 20]} /> // not 8n
```

## Card body padding

- Flush tables only: `company-table-card-body` → `0`.
- Table beside list: `company-table-card-body-inset` → **12px** (Ant `Card` `size="small"`, matches list card).
- List scroll body: `.company-scroll-card-body-fill` → **12px**.

## List & link alignment

Ant Design `Button type="link|text"` defaults to `justify-content: center`. In list rows that stretches content and misaligns titles vs tags.

- Use `.company-list-stack` for title + meta columns in `Listy` rows.
- Task title links: `.company-task-link` (full-width, left-aligned).
- Inline CTA links (Ask Hozie): `.company-inline-link` (auto width, left-aligned).
- Project rows: `.company-project-row` must use `justify-content: flex-start`.
- Never rely on centered link buttons inside list card bodies.
